From 7bfb2c5ef430b1edb72633716e9514987e492c0b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Reixo <125610085+Reixo0@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 22:48:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 04/19] power: supply: qcom_battmgr: Report charge capacity on
 SM8350-style firmware

Only the SC8280XP-style battery info message carries the capacity unit,
so on the SM8350-style protocol (also used by SM8550 and Kaanapali)
battmgr->unit stays at its zero value, QCOM_BATTMGR_UNIT_mWh. As a
result charge_full and charge_full_design always return -ENODATA, even
though the values are requested and received.

That protocol reports capacities in uAh, like charge_counter, so set the
unit to mAh for those variants.

Tested on a Nubia RedMagic 11 Pro (Kaanapali): charge_full and
charge_full_design now match what the downstream kernel reports.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
index 636d6f6ac..676b9a98d 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
@@ -1685,6 +1685,15 @@ static int qcom_battmgr_probe(struct auxiliary_device *adev,
 	else
 		battmgr->variant = QCOM_BATTMGR_SM8350;
 
+	/*
+	 * Only the SC8280XP-style battery info message carries the unit. The
+	 * SM8350-style protocol reports capacities in uAh (like charge_counter),
+	 * so without this charge_full and charge_full_design return -ENODATA.
+	 */
+	if (battmgr->variant != QCOM_BATTMGR_SC8280XP &&
+	    battmgr->variant != QCOM_BATTMGR_X1E80100)
+		battmgr->unit = QCOM_BATTMGR_UNIT_mAh;
+
 	ret = qcom_battmgr_charge_control_thresholds_init(battmgr);
 	if (ret < 0)
 		return dev_err_probe(dev, ret,
